# ── Tooling local state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Claude Code per-user state — the leading-dot variant the IDE writes.
# Ignore everything under .claude EXCEPT shared skills, which are committed
# so teammates get them on checkout. Using `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`) means
# the directory itself isn't excluded, so the `!` carve-out below can
# re-include the skills subtree.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Build outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
*.tar.gz

# NOTE: most dataSet/ and database/ fixtures are intentionally tracked in
# this private repo so teammates clone a working snapshot. Sensitive runtime
# artifacts have explicit exceptions below; put new secrets in .env.
#
# Frontend env files: .env.production is tracked (it's baked into the
# deployed bundle — public by design). .env (host-specific) is NOT
# tracked anymore, so a server's local copy survives `git pull`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Profile photos are biometric PII — never commit them, even though the
# rest of database/ is tracked (see NOTE above).
database/media/
# Legacy camera migration input may contain RTSP credentials. PostgreSQL is
# now the runtime source of truth; never add a new local roster to Git.
database/cameras.json
!frontend/.env.production
*.pem
*.key
notes.txt
